WEBVTT

00:00:23.629 --> 00:00:26.929
Black Diamond fighting. I mean, they're friends. It doesn't make any sense.

00:00:26.929 --> 00:00:28.929
Didn't you read issue 126?

00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:32.630
No, I didn't have any money that week. Why, what happened?

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.130
Okay, so you know how Black Diamond's father is like this super villain, right?

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:40.130
Well, in 126, he busts out of jail, and Warrior Angel has to take him down.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:43.130
But there's this accident, and the guy dies.

00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:53.140
Look what is, boys.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.140
Weirdo Angel and his trusty sidekick grease bottle.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.140
Yeah, I like that.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.140
Give it back, Ollie.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.140
That's Mr. Queen to you, little man.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:07.140
It's okay, Lex. I'll just get another one.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.140
Yeah, Duncan'll just get another one.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.140
Oh, wait. He can.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.140
Oh yeah, that's right. His mommy doesn't have any money.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.140
That's why he's on scholarship.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.140
Shut up, Jeff. Shut up, Alden.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.769
Give it back, Mr. Queen.

00:01:26.769 --> 00:01:27.769
Oh.

00:01:27.769 --> 00:01:28.769
Sure.

00:01:28.769 --> 00:01:30.769
Sure.

00:01:30.769 --> 00:01:31.769
You know what?

00:01:31.769 --> 00:01:34.769
Let's make this a two-part.

00:01:34.769 --> 00:01:38.519
Whoa!

00:01:38.519 --> 00:01:39.519
Oh!

00:01:39.519 --> 00:01:41.519
Nice haircut, Kewball.

00:01:41.519 --> 00:01:48.609
Come on.

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:49.609
These girls aren't even worth it.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:02:19.580
One day, I'm gonna get those guys.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.580
We had a stuffed crow at Smallville, hi.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.580
Two different worlds, huh?

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:31.710
In this case, I think I prefer yours.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.710
If that's how you feel, why come to this thing?

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.710
Oh, Lana, some of the deepest pockets in the country went to Excelsia.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:40.710
These alumni socials are good for business.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:44.710
Well, then let's be social so we can get the hell out of here.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:45.710
Lana!

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:48.710
You're billionaire drag you to this thing, too?

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.710
Oliver's here?

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:51.710
I don't get it.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.710
You put a bunch of pubescent boys in silly jackets

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.710
and cram them full of pomp and circumstance.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.710
You're just asking for a round a lord of the flies.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.710
I don't know.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:06.099
We all turned out all right, didn't we?

00:03:06.099 --> 00:03:07.099
Hey.

00:03:07.099 --> 00:03:11.500
I can only speak for myself.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:17.979
Jeffrey Alden?

00:03:17.979 --> 00:03:18.979
How's business?

00:03:18.979 --> 00:03:20.979
Not as good as you, but hey.

00:03:20.979 --> 00:03:24.680
And you guys were all friends?

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.120
Something like that.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.120
Man, after ten years, gang's all here.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.120
Except for Duncan.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:39.409
Who's Duncan?

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:44.939
What, maybe you ought to lay off, huh?

00:03:44.939 --> 00:03:46.939
Well, like you weren't all thinking about.

00:03:46.939 --> 00:03:47.939
Baldwin.

00:03:47.939 --> 00:03:48.939
Come on.

00:03:48.939 --> 00:03:50.939
Yeah, whatever.

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:54.409
Good to see, Alex.

00:03:54.409 --> 00:04:11.639
You're all right for yourself.

00:04:11.639 --> 00:04:13.639
Duncan, if you were here, it's still here.

00:04:13.639 --> 00:04:15.639
It'd still be a loser.

00:04:15.639 --> 00:04:27.519
You all right?

00:04:27.519 --> 00:04:28.519
Just miss me.

00:04:28.519 --> 00:04:34.100
Must be my lucky day.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:05:52.649
A little dry cleaning won't cure.

00:05:52.649 --> 00:05:55.649
That's distasteful, Lex, even for you.

00:05:55.649 --> 00:05:58.930
What can I say?

00:05:58.930 --> 00:05:59.930
It's a nice suit.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:06.220
You weren't Alden's close friend, Lex, but still...

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:09.220
Well, I should muster up some tears anyway.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.220
Thanks, but I'll save them for someone who deserves it.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:16.269
I know, I know.

00:06:16.269 --> 00:06:18.269
Your life at Excelsior wasn't easy.

00:06:18.269 --> 00:06:22.990
I know that memories can haunt us.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:24.990
can haunt us.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:27.990
But the best way to deal with them is to leave them behind us.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:28.990
Burry them.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:29.990
Where they belong.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:41.139
Along with everything else.

00:06:41.139 --> 00:06:48.259
You're all right.

00:06:48.259 --> 00:06:49.259
If you need anything,

00:06:49.259 --> 00:06:59.579
I won't.

00:06:59.579 --> 00:07:02.579
Perhaps Miss Lang will have better luck comforting you.

00:07:02.579 --> 00:07:29.589
Get out of here.

00:07:29.589 --> 00:07:30.589
I don't know.

00:07:30.589 --> 00:07:31.589
College, I guess.

00:07:31.589 --> 00:07:32.589
Then what?

00:07:32.589 --> 00:07:35.589
My dad wants me to learn how to run his business.

00:07:35.589 --> 00:07:37.589
Are you gonna do it?

00:07:37.589 --> 00:07:39.589
Hell no.

00:07:39.589 --> 00:07:41.589
Can't stand that old bastard.

00:07:41.589 --> 00:07:44.290
What about you?

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.290
What are you gonna do?

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:49.290
I'm gonna help people like Warrior Angel.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:51.290
Better hit the gym.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.290
Spandex and stuff to pull off.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:56.290
No, no, I don't mean like the cape and stuff.

00:07:56.290 --> 00:08:00.290
I'm talking like a doctor or a lawyer or something.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.290
Lawyer?

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.290
Yeah.

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.290
Working pro bono for the poor.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:08.290
Don't let my dad hear you say that.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:10.290
Why? What's your dad against poor people?

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.290
Everything.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.290
He thinks poverty is just another word.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:16.290
for lazy.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:21.680
What do you think?

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.680
I think it would drive my dad nuts

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.680
if I got a job working with the poor.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:31.069
Got room for a partner?

00:08:31.069 --> 00:08:33.070
Elmire and Luther?

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.070
Luther and Ellen Meyer.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.070
Deal.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:09:10.019
Now all we gotta do is graduate one piece.

00:09:10.019 --> 00:09:12.019
What are they doing?

00:09:12.019 --> 00:09:14.019
Stealing answers to the midterms.

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:30.399
You know, you really didn't have to go to all this trouble, Mrs. Kent.

00:09:30.399 --> 00:09:33.399
You can't live on coffee three meals a day, Chloe.

00:09:33.399 --> 00:09:34.399
I'm mix it up.

00:09:34.399 --> 00:09:36.399
with the occasional blueberry muffin?

00:09:36.399 --> 00:09:38.399
What? That has a food group in it?

00:09:38.399 --> 00:09:39.399
Barely.

00:09:39.399 --> 00:09:41.399
Did you find anything new?

00:09:41.399 --> 00:09:42.399
Tons.

00:09:42.399 --> 00:09:46.399
There have been reports of unusual occurrences happening all over the world.

00:09:46.399 --> 00:09:49.399
It's like the Wall of Weird went global.

00:09:49.399 --> 00:09:52.399
The worst attack was on a small village in the Kashmary region of India.

00:09:52.399 --> 00:09:58.789
The entire village was nearly destroyed.

00:09:58.789 --> 00:10:01.789
Villagers said they saw something fall from the sky the night before.

00:10:01.789 --> 00:10:08.279
That's the same time I escaped from the Phantom Zone.

00:10:08.279 --> 00:10:10.279
Do you think whatever it was got out when you escaped?

00:10:10.279 --> 00:10:11.279
Like that part?

00:10:11.279 --> 00:10:13.279
Park Ranger.

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:15.279
How about a trip to the ice castle?

00:10:15.279 --> 00:10:18.279
Maybe Jarrell could help track down the Zoners before they do any more damage.

00:10:18.279 --> 00:10:20.279
Zoners?

00:10:20.279 --> 00:10:24.279
Escaped super criminals from the Phantom Zones, a little bit of a mouthful.

00:10:24.279 --> 00:10:25.279
Fortress is dead.

00:10:25.279 --> 00:10:27.279
There's no contact, Jarrell.

00:10:27.279 --> 00:10:29.279
As for his help.

00:10:29.279 --> 00:10:31.279
I should have just listened to him.

00:10:31.279 --> 00:10:32.279
And done what, Clark?

00:10:32.279 --> 00:10:35.279
Killed Lex to stop Zod from taking over his body?

00:10:35.279 --> 00:10:37.279
You're not a murderer, Clark.

00:10:37.279 --> 00:10:40.279
What about all those people in that village, Mom?

00:10:40.279 --> 00:10:41.279
They might have died.

00:10:41.279 --> 00:10:42.279
because of my actions.

00:10:42.279 --> 00:10:47.740
I need to know for sure.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:50.740
Then we need to find more crater impacts.

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:53.740
Like the one you made when you came out of the Phantom Zone?

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:55.740
I think our best bet would be satellite images.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:58.740
I thought all the satellites were down on Dark Thursday.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:00.740
All except for a few owned by Queen Industries.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:05.740
Now, if we could get the access codes, I might be able to find an image of whatever it is

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:08.740
that came down before the attack on that village.

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:11.740
Oliver Queen still owes me one.

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:18.019
Maybe it's time to collect.

00:11:18.019 --> 00:11:19.019
Seen somebody laugh.

00:11:19.019 --> 00:11:22.019
with shared so many good times together.

00:11:22.019 --> 00:11:25.019
Seeing him laid out on the table like that.

00:11:25.019 --> 00:11:28.019
At least they say he didn't suffer.

00:11:28.019 --> 00:11:31.019
Yeah, but I'm guessing you didn't tickle either.

00:11:31.019 --> 00:11:33.019
Alden called me a month ago.

00:11:33.019 --> 00:11:39.549
Said he wanted to go off for a drink and I told him I was busy.

00:11:39.549 --> 00:11:41.549
Said I'd catch up with him later.

00:11:41.549 --> 00:11:44.549
You couldn't have known something like this was going to happen.

00:11:44.549 --> 00:11:48.960
All the more reason to live for today.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:53.200
Keep in touch with old friends.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.200
Why don't you all get together while you're here?

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.200
while you're here.

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:58.860
And what about that Duncan guy?

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:06.679
Does he live in Metropolis?

00:12:06.679 --> 00:12:07.679
Not anymore.

00:12:07.679 --> 00:12:09.679
I actually have to be getting back to Gotham.

00:12:09.679 --> 00:12:10.679
Anyway.

00:12:10.679 --> 00:12:14.600
Got a great gal there, Ollie.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:15.600
Don't screw it out.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:49.370
Our guy.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.370
You should listen to him.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.370
I'm all ears.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:13:37.159
My security system would keep someone like you out.

00:13:37.159 --> 00:13:39.159
Looks like you need an upgrade.

00:13:39.159 --> 00:13:41.159
Or you need to learn how to knock.

00:13:41.159 --> 00:13:43.159
It's okay. You know what? You can keep that arrow.

00:13:43.159 --> 00:13:47.820
I've got a new one.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:49.820
I was thinking about developing a boxing glove arrow.

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:50.820
And then I thought,

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:51.820
come up with something a little fancy.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:14:14.480
Contained electromagnetic pulse knocks out everything electrical within an eight-foot radius.

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:18.480
Cameras, laser systems, pacemakers.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:20.480
The last one was a Joe Clark.

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:24.179
I'm laughing on the inside.

00:14:24.179 --> 00:14:27.179
Maybe we'll get lucky one day and it'll bubble to the surface.

00:14:27.179 --> 00:14:29.179
To what do I owe the pleasure?

00:14:29.179 --> 00:14:31.179
I need to talk to you about Queen Industries.

00:14:31.179 --> 00:14:32.179
Their satellite grid.

00:14:32.179 --> 00:14:35.549
What about it?

00:14:35.549 --> 00:14:39.549
My friend Chloe, she's doing a story on the global effects of Dark Thursday.

00:14:39.549 --> 00:14:41.549
She needs satellite images from that day, but none of them are working.

00:14:41.549 --> 00:14:43.549
but none of them are working.

00:14:43.549 --> 00:14:44.549
Except mine.

00:14:44.549 --> 00:14:46.549
Now, how'd you manage that?

00:14:46.549 --> 00:14:48.549
It's a trade secret.

00:14:48.549 --> 00:14:50.549
Tell you what.

00:14:50.549 --> 00:14:53.549
I'll give your friend Chloe the access codes to the Grid Archive

00:14:53.549 --> 00:14:56.549
if you do one small thing for me.

00:14:56.549 --> 00:14:57.549
What would that be?

00:14:57.549 --> 00:15:02.549
Help me figure out how Lex caused the accidental death of two of my friends.

00:15:02.549 --> 00:15:04.549
But you think Lex killed them?

00:15:04.549 --> 00:15:07.549
I've known Lex a lot longer than you, Clark.

00:15:07.549 --> 00:15:10.549
I've seen who he really is.

00:15:10.549 --> 00:15:20.669
I'm just saying that you should.

00:15:20.669 --> 00:15:21.669
Think about this.

00:15:21.669 --> 00:15:22.669
What's there to think about?

00:15:22.669 --> 00:15:24.669
We tell the headmaster what we saw,

00:15:24.669 --> 00:15:26.669
and then Queen, those two jerks are out of here.

00:15:26.669 --> 00:15:29.669
But we have something on Queen now.

00:15:29.669 --> 00:15:32.669
No way is he ever going to try anything again?

00:15:32.669 --> 00:15:41.769
Force him to act like our friend so we can have some respect in this place.

00:15:41.769 --> 00:15:47.620
You don't pretend to be friends with somebody likes.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:50.620
You either are or you aren't.

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:58.259
I'm going to turn them in.

00:15:58.259 --> 00:16:08.860
I thought you said you were going to handle this.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:09.860
You told them?

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:14.529
This is our chance, Duncan.

00:16:14.529 --> 00:16:19.799
You don't have to be on the outside anymore.

00:16:19.799 --> 00:16:20.799
I...

00:16:20.799 --> 00:16:23.799
I never felt that way, not when you were my friend.

00:16:23.799 --> 00:16:25.799
Just listen to me.

00:16:25.799 --> 00:16:26.799
Get out of my way.

00:16:26.799 --> 00:16:29.529
Hey!

00:16:29.529 --> 00:16:31.529
What do you think you're going?

00:16:31.529 --> 00:16:34.529
Just keep your rounds shut and everything will be okay.

00:16:34.529 --> 00:16:36.529
Get off of me!

00:16:36.529 --> 00:16:44.950
Get off of me!

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:48.779
These suck a loser!

00:16:48.779 --> 00:16:53.309
Why can you think like everybody else?

00:16:53.309 --> 00:16:54.309
Are you okay?

00:16:54.309 --> 00:16:58.190
Bad dream?

00:16:58.190 --> 00:17:00.190
What was it about?

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:02.190
I don't remember.

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:08.539
Lex, it's normal to be upset. Alden died right in front of you.

00:17:08.539 --> 00:17:11.539
Yeah, well, maybe he finally got what he deserved.

00:17:11.539 --> 00:17:13.539
How can you say that about your friend?

00:17:13.539 --> 00:17:18.839
I only had one friend that excelsior.

00:17:18.839 --> 00:17:20.839
And it sure as hell wasn't him.

00:17:20.839 --> 00:17:22.839
Do you want to talk about it?

00:17:22.839 --> 00:17:32.809
Not really.

00:17:32.809 --> 00:17:47.700
And the last thing you have to worry about.

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:51.779
The last thing, huh?

00:17:51.779 --> 00:17:52.779
Well, at least it didn't break.

00:17:52.779 --> 00:18:04.500
Did you see that?

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.500
I'm sure it's nothing to worry about, Lana.

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:20.470
See?

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:26.460
Lex.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:57.400
Stay in a fairly serious concussion, but the cat's cancer negative.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:58.400
A couple of days rest.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:18:59.400
She'll be fine.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:00.400
I'll make sure she gets it.

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:04.890
Where's Lana?

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:05.890
She'll be fine.

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:07.890
That's the only thing that matters.

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:09.890
I want to talk to her.

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:11.890
You lost your visiting rights a while back, Clark.

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:18.630
I wouldn't be here if it wasn't for you, Lex.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:21.630
Since you've been with her, she has a funny habit of getting hurt.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:24.630
And how many times did she wind up in the hospital when she was dating you?

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:36.480
Save yourself a trip next time.

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.480
You got yourself a trip next time, Clark.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:46.369
Just send flowers.

00:19:46.369 --> 00:19:47.369
That was harsh.

00:19:47.369 --> 00:19:52.309
It's not like he's wrong, though.

00:19:52.309 --> 00:19:53.309
I've heard Lana more than anyone else.

00:19:53.309 --> 00:19:55.309
She wouldn't even be with Lex if it wasn't for me.

00:19:55.309 --> 00:19:57.309
Lana made that questionable choice on her own.

00:19:57.309 --> 00:19:59.309
Stop beating yourself up.

00:19:59.309 --> 00:20:00.309
It's my job.

00:20:00.309 --> 00:20:04.819
And my other one is sniffing out a good story.

00:20:04.819 --> 00:20:06.819
That's why you're here?

00:20:06.819 --> 00:20:09.819
I don't think Lana's chandelier run-in was an accident.

00:20:09.819 --> 00:20:11.819
Or that she was the target.

00:20:11.819 --> 00:20:14.819
In the past 24 hours, two of Lex and Oliver's old friends

00:20:14.819 --> 00:20:17.819
from boarding school died in violent accidents.

00:20:17.819 --> 00:20:20.819
And you think Lex was almost the third?

00:20:20.819 --> 00:20:23.819
I think it has something to do with a kid named Dunk and they all knew,

00:20:23.819 --> 00:20:25.819
but Oliver won't tell me anything.

00:20:25.819 --> 00:20:30.160
Listen, I don't want you to end up sharing a hospital room with Lana, right?

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.160
Get some distance between you and Oliver, just for now.

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:36.160
Or I could man up and get to the bottom of this like a real reporter,

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:40.160
preferably before the Grim Reaper drop something very heavy on my hot boyfriend.

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:54.160
Is Lana gonna be okay?

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:56.160
I think so.

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:58.160
We'll take you wrong about Lex being the one

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:00.160
behind the attacks.

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:03.160
Unless he orchestrated this one to throw off suspicion.

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:05.160
If Lex was the only one hurt,

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.730
then I probably think the same thing.

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:10.730
He loves Lana too much to risk her life.

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:17.690
If these attacks aren't random,

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:24.940
Lois seems to think it may have something to do

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:26.940
with the kid you went to school with back at Excelsior.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:27.940
Duncan?

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:31.400
It's not Duncan.

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:33.400
How can you be sure?

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:42.769
Because Lex and I killed him 10 years ago.

00:21:42.769 --> 00:21:44.769
Why are you being just a reason?

00:21:44.769 --> 00:21:45.769
Lex!

00:21:45.769 --> 00:21:46.769
Let's stop it!

00:21:46.769 --> 00:21:47.769
What are you doing?

00:21:47.769 --> 00:21:48.769
Lex!

00:21:48.769 --> 00:21:56.170
Stop!

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:57.170
Dude.

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.170
Say how much?

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:03.539
There's something seriously wrong with you.

00:22:03.539 --> 00:22:18.980
Duncan!

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.980
Get away from me!

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:29.490
You want to be one of them so badly, Lex?

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:30.490
Is that it?

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:33.490
You can't stand being a loser like me?

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:35.490
Well, congratulations, buddy.

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:37.490
Now you're their friend.

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:38.490
And you can have...

00:22:38.490 --> 00:22:40.490
Duncan!

00:22:40.490 --> 00:22:42.490
Oh, my God!

00:22:42.490 --> 00:22:51.339
Duncan suffered massive brain injuries.

00:22:51.339 --> 00:22:54.339
Is there anything else that you haven't told me?

00:22:54.339 --> 00:22:59.440
Just the denouement?

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:04.440
Lionel Luther sweeping in with the best doctors in the world save Duncan.

00:23:04.440 --> 00:23:06.440
Lionel.

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:09.440
I thought it was an act of kindness.

00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:13.440
Now that I'm older, I realize it was just an act.

00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:17.440
Lionel was trying to cover up what happened between Lex and Duncan.

00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:21.440
Trying to cover up the stink off the Luther name.

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:25.359
How do you know about all this?

00:23:25.359 --> 00:23:26.359
You got the whole story from Ler.

00:23:26.359 --> 00:23:32.200
Duncan was on scholarship.

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:34.200
His parents couldn't afford a band-aid,

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:36.200
let alone a team of neurosurgeons.

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:39.200
So Lionel promised to take care of the whole thing.

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:41.200
As long as everyone kept quiet.

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:43.200
Not that it mattered.

00:23:43.200 --> 00:23:48.460
Duncan died two days later.

00:23:48.460 --> 00:23:49.460
It was an accident.

00:23:49.460 --> 00:23:51.460
It just happened.

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:55.000
No.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:57.000
No, I told myself that same life for years.

00:23:57.000 --> 00:24:02.980
The truth is, all of us might as well have pushed them out in front of that car.

00:24:02.980 --> 00:24:04.980
Alden, Jeffrey, Lex,

00:24:04.980 --> 00:24:06.980
Me.

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:22.579
We all killed Duncan Ellen Meyer.

00:24:22.579 --> 00:24:24.579
What about his family?

00:24:24.579 --> 00:24:26.579
If they believe you killed him, one of them might be behind this.

00:24:26.579 --> 00:24:29.579
I thought about that, but the only relative I could find was his mother.

00:24:29.579 --> 00:24:30.579
Where's she?

00:24:30.579 --> 00:24:36.890
Granville Cemetery. She passed away a month ago.

00:24:36.890 --> 00:24:38.890
There must be someone else. Someone else you may have missed.

00:24:38.890 --> 00:24:42.809
I don't know.

00:24:42.809 --> 00:24:45.809
The only one who had contact with Duncan's family was Lionel.

00:24:45.809 --> 00:24:47.809
I'm not exactly high on his buddy list.

00:24:47.809 --> 00:24:49.809
Not a good chance of him talking to me.

00:24:49.809 --> 00:25:08.160
I was just on my...

00:25:08.160 --> 00:25:09.160
uh...

00:25:09.160 --> 00:25:12.160
Way down the street to Pestis for lunch.

00:25:12.160 --> 00:25:13.160
You hungry?

00:25:13.160 --> 00:25:15.160
No, this isn't a social visit.

00:25:15.160 --> 00:25:16.160
Oh, it's a pity.

00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:21.160
The owner's wife does a sufleo frommage that is a...

00:25:21.160 --> 00:25:23.160
well, it is out of this world.

00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:29.859
Duncan Ellen, Mike.

00:25:29.859 --> 00:25:31.859
How do you know that name?

00:25:31.859 --> 00:25:32.859
Oliver Queen filled me in.

00:25:32.859 --> 00:25:35.859
Ah, yes, the Queen boy.

00:25:35.859 --> 00:25:38.859
You should know better than to dig up old skeletons.

00:25:38.859 --> 00:25:41.859
Not sure he's the only one with a shovel in his hand.

00:25:41.859 --> 00:25:42.859
He's attacked.

00:25:42.859 --> 00:25:46.859
These attacks, I think someone who was close to Duncan is trying to settle a score.

00:25:46.859 --> 00:25:48.859
Lex was the only one close to him.

00:25:48.859 --> 00:25:51.859
No other family members, besides his mother.

00:25:51.859 --> 00:25:52.859
Didn't have any.

00:25:52.859 --> 00:25:54.859
There's got to be someone.

00:25:54.859 --> 00:26:02.049
What is it you're not telling me?

00:26:02.049 --> 00:26:04.049
Two people are already dead.

00:26:04.049 --> 00:26:06.049
Do you want to add Lex the body count?

00:26:06.049 --> 00:26:09.049
Now please, tell me.

00:26:09.049 --> 00:26:19.450
It was a tragedy what happened to Duncan.

00:26:19.450 --> 00:26:26.220
I did everything possible to help him.

00:26:26.220 --> 00:26:27.220
I have continued to do that.

00:26:27.220 --> 00:26:30.220
to do that for the past 10 years.

00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:32.220
Duncan's alive?

00:26:32.220 --> 00:26:34.220
My medical team was able to keep his heart beating,

00:26:34.220 --> 00:26:38.220
but the injuries from his accident

00:26:38.220 --> 00:26:42.220
have left him in a permanent, vegetative state.

00:26:42.220 --> 00:26:45.539
Why did you let everyone believe he was still dead?

00:26:45.539 --> 00:26:50.789
Clark.

00:26:50.789 --> 00:26:59.109
I didn't want Lex to be crippled by his mistakes.

00:26:59.109 --> 00:27:03.109
I decided to make an arrangement with Duncan's mother

00:27:03.109 --> 00:27:06.109
in exchange for her silence, going along with the story.

00:27:06.109 --> 00:27:11.109
I agreed to fund a research program dedicated to

00:27:11.109 --> 00:27:16.109
reversing the damage to her son's brain.

00:27:16.109 --> 00:27:21.789
This is still going on?

00:27:21.789 --> 00:27:23.789
The best research minds in the world

00:27:23.789 --> 00:27:26.789
have tried hundreds of different treatments, but...

00:27:26.789 --> 00:27:27.789
What if one of them worked?

00:27:27.789 --> 00:28:10.339
It's time for your treatment, Duncan?

00:28:10.339 --> 00:28:41.750
I'm following the lead. I checked out Duncan's mother.

00:28:41.750 --> 00:28:42.750
She's dead.

00:28:42.750 --> 00:28:44.750
I know that, Sherlock.

00:28:44.750 --> 00:28:46.750
On a hunch, I dug up all her old phone records.

00:28:46.750 --> 00:28:47.750
And every day while she was still kicking,

00:28:47.750 --> 00:28:48.750
she placed.

00:28:48.750 --> 00:28:49.750
to call to this facility.

00:28:49.750 --> 00:28:51.750
She's checking on her son.

00:28:51.750 --> 00:28:52.750
Duncan?

00:28:52.750 --> 00:28:54.750
I thought he was dead.

00:28:54.750 --> 00:28:56.750
Yeah, so did everyone else.

00:28:56.750 --> 00:28:58.750
I think he's in this room.

00:28:58.750 --> 00:29:00.750
How do you know all this?

00:29:00.750 --> 00:29:03.750
You're not the only one with hunches.

00:29:03.750 --> 00:29:05.750
Nice work.

00:29:05.750 --> 00:29:06.750
Lois?

00:29:06.750 --> 00:29:16.369
My story, I don't share bylines.

00:29:16.369 --> 00:29:19.369
It's locked.

00:29:19.369 --> 00:29:26.619
You stay here, I'm going to flirt us at a set of keys, right?

00:29:26.619 --> 00:29:27.619
Lois.

00:29:27.619 --> 00:29:30.319
It's just stuck.

00:29:30.319 --> 00:29:44.930
Ladies first.

00:29:44.930 --> 00:29:48.490
Yes.

00:29:48.490 --> 00:29:56.240
Thank you.

00:29:56.240 --> 00:29:58.240
Lex, I was wondering how long it was going to take you to pop up.

00:29:58.240 --> 00:30:01.619
I've been busy.

00:30:01.619 --> 00:30:03.619
At the hospital.

00:30:03.619 --> 00:30:05.619
I heard about Lana.

00:30:05.619 --> 00:30:06.619
Is she going to be all right?

00:30:06.619 --> 00:30:08.619
She'll be fine.

00:30:08.619 --> 00:30:10.619
Not that you really care.

00:30:10.619 --> 00:30:12.619
No, I do care.

00:30:12.619 --> 00:30:19.369
I care that a nice girl like that ended up with a guy like you.

00:30:19.369 --> 00:30:21.369
Ever since you came to Metropolis,

00:30:21.369 --> 00:30:26.369
I've been kidnapped, my life put in jeopardy, and now the woman I love is lying in a hospital,

00:30:26.369 --> 00:30:28.369
And you think that's my fault.

00:30:28.369 --> 00:30:31.900
Sounds to me more like bad karma.

00:30:31.900 --> 00:30:34.900
Go back to Star City, Oliver.

00:30:34.900 --> 00:30:37.900
Why, you still can't.

00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:41.730
I've seen that look before.

00:30:41.730 --> 00:30:44.619
When was it?

00:30:44.619 --> 00:30:47.700
Oh yeah.

00:30:47.700 --> 00:30:52.009
When you almost beat your only friend at death back at Excelsior?

00:30:52.009 --> 00:31:07.480
The first one's free.

00:31:07.480 --> 00:31:14.980
The next one's gonna cost you.

00:31:14.980 --> 00:31:15.980
Poor little Lex.

00:31:15.980 --> 00:31:18.980
I was blaming everyone else for all of his problems.

00:31:18.980 --> 00:31:20.980
Only when they're the cause.

00:31:20.980 --> 00:31:29.630
Never could take responsibility for what happened to

00:31:29.650 --> 00:31:30.650
Duncan.

00:31:30.650 --> 00:31:32.650
Like your hands were clean.

00:31:32.650 --> 00:31:34.650
Not even close.

00:31:34.650 --> 00:31:37.650
But since then, I've been scrubbing them real hard.

00:31:37.650 --> 00:31:55.170
Yours just keep getting dirtier.

00:31:55.170 --> 00:32:21.859
Lex.

00:32:21.859 --> 00:32:23.859
I'm not a doctor, but I've seen enough Discovery Channel

00:32:23.859 --> 00:32:26.859
to know you don't get the squiggly lines when you're in a vegetative state.

00:32:26.859 --> 00:32:29.859
Unless your new treatments are working.

00:32:29.859 --> 00:32:31.859
What new treatment?

00:32:31.859 --> 00:32:35.859
There's something called 12B. It's experimental.

00:32:35.859 --> 00:32:37.859
It's derived from refined meteor rocks.

00:32:37.859 --> 00:32:39.859
Clark, they started giving him this stuff two days ago.

00:32:39.859 --> 00:32:41.859
this stuff two days ago.

00:32:41.859 --> 00:32:43.859
Look at the injection times.

00:32:43.859 --> 00:32:45.859
It coincide with the attacks.

00:32:45.859 --> 00:32:47.859
Maybe we just found our killer.

00:32:47.859 --> 00:32:51.859
Wait a minute. These treatments, they might stimulate brain activity, but he's still in a wheelchair.

00:32:51.859 --> 00:32:54.859
His body is, yeah, but look at his charts.

00:32:54.859 --> 00:32:58.859
His new cocktail is whipping up a hell of an electrical storm.

00:32:58.859 --> 00:33:02.859
Now, I read this article in The Inquisitor about brainwaves and astral projection.

00:33:02.859 --> 00:33:04.859
Astral projection.

00:33:04.859 --> 00:33:07.859
Do you have a better explanation?

00:33:07.859 --> 00:33:08.859
No.

00:33:08.859 --> 00:33:09.859
When was his life?

00:33:09.859 --> 00:33:12.299
Last injection.

00:33:12.299 --> 00:33:13.299
Twenty minutes ago.

00:33:13.299 --> 00:34:23.179
A small, though, I...

00:34:23.179 --> 00:34:25.179
Well, things heated up, as usual.

00:34:25.179 --> 00:34:28.179
I went to go find a phone to warn Oliver and Lex.

00:34:28.179 --> 00:34:31.179
Did you get a hold of them? Are they all right?

00:34:31.179 --> 00:34:35.179
Well, worse for where. Oliver said whatever happened just suddenly stopped.

00:34:35.179 --> 00:34:38.179
Well, Duncan went flatline, like he blew a fuse or something.

00:34:38.179 --> 00:34:40.179
I wonder what caused it.

00:34:40.179 --> 00:34:43.550
You need that for your article?

00:34:43.550 --> 00:34:46.550
Well, it would be good if I were still going to write one.

00:34:46.550 --> 00:34:48.550
But you're not?

00:34:48.550 --> 00:34:49.550
It would make a juicy story.

00:34:49.550 --> 00:34:54.550
A juicy story for the inquisitor, but considering the outcome,

00:34:54.550 --> 00:35:00.550
an exploitation piece on a catatonic patient astro projecting his way to revenge might be in bad taste.

00:35:00.550 --> 00:35:05.550
Would you still feel the same way if Oliver wasn't involved?

00:35:05.550 --> 00:35:07.550
We've all done things we're not proud of.

00:35:07.550 --> 00:35:11.550
I just wish that Oliver didn't feel like he had to hide it from me.

00:35:11.550 --> 00:35:20.340
You know, sometimes in order to protect the people we love, we keep secrets.

00:35:20.340 --> 00:35:26.039
Totally retarded.

00:35:26.039 --> 00:35:27.039
retarded.

00:35:27.039 --> 00:35:46.039
I wasn't the most popular kid at Excelsior.

00:35:46.039 --> 00:35:48.039
The way I looked.

00:35:48.039 --> 00:35:51.039
The rumors about what happened to my brother, Julian,

00:35:51.039 --> 00:35:56.139
but Duncan didn't care.

00:35:56.139 --> 00:36:02.730
He was my only friend, and I betrayed him.

00:36:02.730 --> 00:36:04.730
Lex, you were just a boy.

00:36:04.730 --> 00:36:07.730
What matters is the man you've become?

00:36:07.730 --> 00:36:25.860
It's not often I get invited into the lion's den.

00:36:25.860 --> 00:36:27.860
I didn't want you changing your mind.

00:36:27.860 --> 00:36:30.860
I'm sure you two have a lot to discuss.

00:36:30.860 --> 00:36:32.860
Mr. Queen?

00:36:32.860 --> 00:36:33.860
Mr. Queen?

00:36:33.860 --> 00:36:39.039
Miss Lang, you're a lucky man.

00:36:39.039 --> 00:36:46.420
In more ways than one.

00:36:46.420 --> 00:36:47.420
I should be dead.

00:36:47.420 --> 00:36:50.820
Here I stand.

00:36:50.820 --> 00:36:53.820
You would have done the same thing for me.

00:36:53.820 --> 00:36:54.820
Right?

00:36:54.820 --> 00:36:56.820
I wanted to say thank you.

00:36:56.820 --> 00:37:01.230
And that's all I wanted to say.

00:37:01.230 --> 00:37:04.230
I'm sure you have business to get back too.

00:37:04.230 --> 00:37:22.829
Lex, what happened to Duncan, the way I treated both of you.

00:37:22.829 --> 00:37:27.809
It's not something that I'm proud of.

00:37:27.809 --> 00:37:28.809
I want you to know how much I regret it.

00:37:28.809 --> 00:37:41.519
And I regret it, ever thinking I needed friends like you.

00:37:41.519 --> 00:38:06.750
Why'd you lie to me?

00:38:06.750 --> 00:38:10.750
All those years you let me think he was dead.

00:38:10.750 --> 00:38:14.829
What would you have done if you'd known the truth?

00:38:14.829 --> 00:38:18.829
Make daily pilgrimages to the poor boy's bedside?

00:38:18.829 --> 00:38:21.829
Yes, I let you think he was dead.

00:38:21.829 --> 00:38:24.829
I was giving you a chance to move on with your life,

00:38:24.829 --> 00:38:26.829
to go forward, not back.

00:38:26.829 --> 00:38:28.829
You didn't do this for me.

00:38:28.829 --> 00:38:30.829
He convinced Duncan's mother to declare.

00:38:30.829 --> 00:38:33.829
Duncan's mother to declare him dead so he could use him as a guinea pig.

00:38:33.829 --> 00:38:37.829
And one of your treatments tapped into a very powerful part of the human brain.

00:38:37.829 --> 00:38:38.829
All right, all right.

00:38:38.829 --> 00:38:40.829
Let's assume that's true.

00:38:40.829 --> 00:38:42.829
Would that have made a difference?

00:38:42.829 --> 00:38:45.829
You were responsible for what happened to Duncan Elman Meyer.

00:38:45.829 --> 00:38:51.650
Nothing has ever going to change that.

00:38:51.650 --> 00:38:56.699
Like you said, Dad, the only thing I can do is look forward.

00:38:56.699 --> 00:39:03.829
I want to see the data on Duncan's last treatment.

00:39:03.829 --> 00:39:16.940
Have it on my desk first thing in the morning.

00:39:16.940 --> 00:39:17.940
So that thing that attacked us.

00:39:17.940 --> 00:39:20.940
Duncan's astral body or whatever you want to call.

00:39:20.940 --> 00:39:22.940
It must have been some form of electrical manifestation.

00:39:22.940 --> 00:39:26.940
I got fried by your electromagnetic arrow along with what was left of Duncan's brain.

00:39:26.940 --> 00:39:31.250
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:39:31.250 --> 00:39:37.510
You know, making the wrong choices and living with the consequences.

00:39:37.510 --> 00:39:39.510
It's not easy, is it?

00:39:39.510 --> 00:39:42.510
Speaking from experience, huh?

00:39:42.510 --> 00:39:44.510
More than I'd like.

00:39:44.510 --> 00:39:53.460
You know, we all make bad choices, Clark.

00:39:53.460 --> 00:39:55.460
All we can do is hope to make the right ones in the future, right?

00:39:55.460 --> 00:40:04.219
I'm sorry, I didn't realize you had company.

00:40:04.219 --> 00:40:05.219
Chloe? Oliver Queen.

00:40:05.219 --> 00:40:07.219
Chloe, Oliver Queen.

00:40:07.219 --> 00:40:12.219
Oh, hi. I feel like I know you already. Lois talks about you all the time.

00:40:12.219 --> 00:40:15.219
I was actually just going to go see Lois right now.

00:40:15.219 --> 00:40:18.219
Maybe it's the time I did some talking.

00:40:18.219 --> 00:40:22.219
Well, look, I'm looking forward to your article on Dark Thursday.

00:40:22.219 --> 00:40:27.829
I hope my satellite images helped?

00:40:27.829 --> 00:40:28.829
Yeah.

00:40:28.829 --> 00:40:30.829
Good. It's good to meet you.

00:40:30.829 --> 00:40:40.289
In person, he is really...

00:40:40.289 --> 00:40:49.130
Chloe, be able to pull anything off the satellites?

00:40:49.130 --> 00:40:50.130
Oh, yeah.

00:40:50.130 --> 00:40:52.130
Um, well, I'm still sifting through the images,

00:40:52.130 --> 00:40:55.130
but I already found a handful of craters

00:40:55.130 --> 00:40:58.130
that matched the one you made when you busted under the Phantom Zone.

00:40:58.130 --> 00:41:02.889
Which means more zoners on Earth.

00:41:02.889 --> 00:41:04.889
Did you find the one in India?

00:41:04.889 --> 00:41:07.889
I was just a smoking hole, but I did find another one in Australia

00:41:07.889 --> 00:41:10.889
that I thought you might want to take a look at.

00:41:10.889 --> 00:41:18.619
Is there someone in a crater?

00:41:18.619 --> 00:41:19.619
I blew it up as much as I could.

00:41:19.619 --> 00:41:21.619
It's not very clear, but...

00:41:21.619 --> 00:41:31.739
What is that?

